		{
			dependencies: ["2AA63D77B0E86D2E"]
			description: [
		"&6&l» Core Mechanism"
		"&f- Neutron kinetic energy is consumed to run the recipe."
		"&f- The neutron kinetic energy must exactly match the limited range of the recipe. It will not work if it is too high or too low."
		"&f- Different formulas require different neutron kinetic energy ranges, so multiple units need to be prepared and configured separately."
		""
		"&6&l» Control method"
		"&f- Use the &bmachine control overlay &fto control the energy input to regulate neutron kinetic energy."
		"&f- Use the &bneutron sensor &fto output a redstone signal to assist in monitoring the neutron kinetic energy range."
		""
		"&6&l» Configuration example"
		"&f- If the recipe requires neutron kinetic energy 220~230:"
		"&a- Sets the sensor's lowest value to &e222 &fand its highest value to &e228 &f."
		"&a- This ensures that the kinetic energy requirements of the formula are always met."
		""
		"&e&l» Warm reminder"
		"&e- Since the range required for each formula is different, it is recommended to prepare separate machines for different formulas."
	]
